#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:1
msgid "Manipulating Models"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:3
msgid ""
"This tutorial will walk you through using various plugins to assist model "
"and scene manipulation in the Ignition GUI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:5
msgid ""
"The Transform Control plugin is a combination of keybindings and transform "
"control options: selection, translation, rotation and snapping. This chart "
"of [Ignition's keyboard shortcuts](hotkeys) may be helpful for this tutorial."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:8
msgid ""
"The View Angle plugin allows you to quickly and easily adjust the direction "
"from which your scene faces an entity in the simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:10
msgid "The Component Inspector plugin displays a variety of object attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:12
msgid ""
"The Align Tool aligns entities along or about a specific entity's bounding "
"box."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:14
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:16
msgid "Start by getting Ignition up and running with a sample world:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:18
msgid "ign gazebo shapes.sdf\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:22
msgid ""
"The previous tutorial, [Understanding the GUI](gui), explains the basics of "
"navigating the Ignition GUI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:24
msgid "Transform Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:26
msgid ""
"The top left toolbar contains controls for transforming. Alternatively, the "
"Transform Control plugin can be selected from the plugin drop-down menu. The "
"plugin will then appear at the bottom of the right panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:30
msgid "![Choosing Transform Control from the plugin list](img/plugins.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:30
msgid "Choosing Transform Control from the plugin list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:32
msgid "Select Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:34
msgid ""
"Selection is the default mode. You can click to select entities in the "
"scene. A selected entity will be highlighted in the Entity Tree to indicate "
"its selection. You can select multiple entities by holding `Ctrl` and "
"clicking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:39
msgid "![Selecting multiple entities](img/select_mult.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:39
msgid "Selecting multiple entities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:41
msgid "Entities can't be manipulated in select mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:43
msgid ""
"You can always return to selection mode from any other mode by pressing "
"`Esc`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:45
msgid "Translate Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:47
msgid ""
"Enter into translate mode by clicking the second icon from the left in the "
"top left toolbar, the Transform Control plugin, or by hitting the keyboard "
"shortcut: `T`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:49
msgid "![Translate mode icon](img/translate_icon.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:49
msgid "Translate mode icon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:51
msgid ""
"Translate mode allows you to translate entities along the x, y and z axes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:53
msgid ""
"Click on any entity while in translate mode to see the arrows representing "
"the axes you can move along. The red arrow represents the x-axis, green the "
"y-axis, and blue the z-axis. Click and hold on any of the arrows while "
"moving your mouse to move the entity in that direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:57
msgid "![Translate mode](img/translate.gif)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:57
msgid "Translate mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:59
msgid ""
"Additionally, holding down any one of the `X`, `Y` or `Z` keys, or a "
"combination of them, while clicking and dragging will constrain the model's "
"movement along those axes, regardless of the direction you move your mouse "
"or the axis arrow you select."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:61
msgid "Rotate Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:63
msgid ""
"Enter into rotate mode by clicking the third icon from the left in the top "
"left toolbar, the Transform Control plugin, or by hitting the keyboard "
"shortcut: `R`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:65
msgid "![Rotate mode icon](img/rotate_icon.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:65
msgid "Rotate mode icon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:67
msgid ""
"Rotate mode allows you to rotate entities around the roll, pitch and yaw "
"axes of rotation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:69
msgid ""
"Click on any entity while in rotate mode to see the circles representing the "
"axes you can rotate along. The red circle represents roll, green is pitch, "
"and blue is yaw. Click and hold on any of the circles while moving your "
"mouse to rotate the entity around that axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:73
msgid "![Rotate mode](img/rotate.gif)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:73
msgid "Rotate mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:75
msgid "Align to World frame"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:77
msgid ""
"An entity's local axes can become unaligned from the world frame after "
"rotation. If you would like to translate along the world frame axis, simply "
"hold `Shift`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:80
msgid ""
"This isn't a permanent realignment; you can move the entity while holding "
"`Shift`, but once you let go it will return to it's local translational "
"frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:82
msgid "![World frame alignment - translation](img/translate_worldframe.gif)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:82
msgid "World frame alignment - translation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:84
msgid "The same can be done for an entity's local rotational frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:86
msgid "![World frame alignment - rotation](img/rotate_worldframe.gif)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:86
msgid "World frame alignment - rotation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:88
msgid "Enter Custom Snap Values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:90
msgid ""
"When translating or rotating, you can \"snap\" an entity's movement to "
"preset increments by holding `Ctrl` and then clicking and dragging. By "
"default, the snap value is 1 meter for translation and 45° for rotation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:93
msgid ""
"Translational snaps will snap relative to the world frame, whereas "
"rotational snaps will snap relative to the object's current orientation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:95
msgid "![Snap rotation](img/snap.gif)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:95
msgid "Snap rotation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:97
msgid ""
"You can customize snap values by clicking on the snap icon ![Snap icon](img/"
"snap_icon.png) in the top left toolbar or the Transform Control plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:97
msgid "Snap icon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:99
msgid "![Custom snap values](img/custom_snap.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:99
msgid "Custom snap values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:101
msgid ""
"Try holding `Shift` and `Ctrl` simultaneously to snap a model along the "
"world frame is if isn't already aligned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:103
msgid "Component Inspector"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:105
msgid ""
"With this plugin, you can select an entity to display some of its "
"attributes, including its pose, whether or not wind is acting on it, whether "
"or not it's static, and more. The plugin also displays the gravitational and "
"magnetic fields of your world."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:108
msgid ""
"Expanding the `Pose` attribute will show the coordinate values for a "
"selected object. The values will update as the object is moved around "
"(translated or rotated) while the simulation is running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:111
msgid "![Updating pose values](img/pose_value.gif)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:111
msgid "Updating pose values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:113
msgid ""
"You can also pause the plugin so an object's pose values don't update in the "
"inspector while the simulation is playing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:115
msgid ""
"Additionally, the Component Inspector can be locked on one object so you can "
"open another Component Inspector to simultaneously observe another object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:117
msgid "![Two Component Inspectors](img/pose2.gif)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:117
msgid "Two Component Inspectors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:119
msgid "View Angle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:121
msgid "Select the View Angle from the plugins drop-down menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:123
msgid ""
"You can choose which angle you want to view the scene from, relative to a "
"selected entity or the world frame if no entity is selected. The home button "
"will return you to the original view pose from when the scene was loaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:126
msgid ""
"You can also select multiple entities to face simultaneously from each view "
"angle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:128
msgid "![View angle for multiple entities](img/view.gif)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:128
msgid "View angle for multiple entities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:130
msgid "Align Tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:132
msgid "Select the Align Tool from the plugins drop-down menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:134
msgid ""
"The Align Tool aligns a model along or about the bounding box of another "
"model, or any other entity that has a bounding box, like a link for example. "
"It can't, however, align a child link or anything other than the top-level "
"model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:137
msgid ""
"With `Relative to First` selected, select two models using `Ctrl` + click "
"(be sure you are in select mode) and then hover over any of the Align Tool "
"buttons to see a preview of the second model aligning to the first along its "
"x, y or z axis. Hovering over the buttons for each axis will show a preview "
"of where the model would end up if aligned along that axis while clicking "
"will confirm that specific alignment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:142
msgid "![Align](img/align.gif)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:142
msgid "Align"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:144
msgid ""
"The Reverse button will enable alignment about the outer boundary of a "
"model's bounding box.  This feature is helpful for placing objects exactly "
"next to each other.  Notice the difference in alignment when the Reverse "
"button is pressed in the gif below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:147
msgid "![Align Reverse](img/align_reverse.gif)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:147
msgid "Align Reverse"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:149
msgid ""
"You can align more than two models as well, simply select more models with "
"`Ctrl` + click. You can select `First` or `Last` in the `Relative to:` drop "
"down menu to choose which entity to align to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:152
msgid "Next Up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manipulating_models.md:154
msgid ""
"So far you've interacted with basic shape models to learn about Ignition's "
"GUI. It's also possible to insert more detailed models from [Ignition Fuel]"
"(https://app.gazebosim.org) into the GUI. Check out the [Model Insertion "
"from Fuel](fuel_insert) tutorial to learn how."
msgstr ""
